@startuml
title MEDORA -- Check In Patient (System Sequence)
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam dpi 192
skinparam backgroundColor #F5F9FE
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultFontColor #183247
skinparam defaultFontSize 16
skinparam titleFontSize 20
skinparam note {
  BackgroundColor #EAF3FB
  BorderColor #2563A6
  FontColor #183247
}
skinparam ArrowColor #2563A6
skinparam sequence {
  ParticipantBackgroundColor #EAF3FB
  ParticipantBorderColor #163A5F
  ParticipantFontColor #183247
  LifeLineBorderColor #2563A6
  LifeLineBackgroundColor #F5F9FE
}
actor Receptionist
participant "MEDORA System" as System

Receptionist -> System: Check in patient(appointment or walk-in)
activate System
alt Request unauthorized or identity unresolved
  System --> Receptionist: Reject; make no encounter change
else Request is valid
  alt Conflicting active encounter
    System --> Receptionist: Reject duplicate; preserve current state
  else No conflicting encounter
    System --> Receptionist: Return encounter and queue status
  end
end
deactivate System
note over Receptionist, System
  Walk-ins follow the facility acceptance policy. An appointment
  alone is not evidence that an encounter has started.
end note
@enduml